    "title"             "Knox Relay"
    "description"       "Server-side bridge mod for remote server management. Exports game state, inventory snapshots, player positions, progression, live character vitals and appearance, and processes item delivery and money deposit queues via file-based JSON communication. Provides /account register for linking a character to a website account, /report for filing a player report from inside the game, and a friends list with optional map pins: right-click a survivor to ask, accept from the Knox Desk or the website."
    "changenote"        "[h1]1.35 — Friend map pins both ways, quieter logs[/h1]\n[b]Fixed[/b]\n[list]\n[*]A friend's last-known position is saved even when the in-game name differs only by case, so their pin still appears after they log out.\n[*]Live positions keep exporting if one player's appearance cannot be read, instead of dropping everyone.\n[*]In-game friend pins still draw when the command channel sends coordinates as strings.\n[*]Holding an axe or other melee weapon no longer throws a Java exception every in-game minute while Knox Relay reads live character stats.\n[*]Firearm ammo, chamber, and jam are only read when those methods exist on the equipped item, so guns still report them and blades do not.\n[*]Opening the Knox Desk no longer throws when a button or list has no paginate method.\n[*]Missing server events such as OnPlayerDisconnect and OnRecipeLearned are skipped at load instead of dumping a Java exception.\n[*]A joining multiplayer client no longer runs the dedicated-server event loop.\n[*]The in-game Mods screen shows the Knox Relay version (1.35) instead of a blank Version row. The same mod.info is in 42/ and common/, which is what PZ reads for that field.\n[/list]"
}
